                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "fbda6c4f-ae5f-4da1-86d0-15a3ae065c3a",
                        "source_entry_id": "bd8f512d-a666-325e-bd52-619cbe9ec433",
                        "target_lang_word": "Hypothese",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Hypothese",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7f9ab0c4-be61-3b76-84fa-b12239ab204c",
                                        "entry_id": "e6eca988-a510-3c3a-b528-9cf4b6d8c9fd",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "unbewiesene (wissenschaftliche) Annahme, die noch eines Beweises bedarf"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Wissenschaft"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1f145852-bbe0-4f7f-bc01-67f213138a0c",
                                                "sense_id": "7f9ab0c4-be61-3b76-84fa-b12239ab204c",
                                                "text": "Hypothesen können induktiv aufgrund von Beobachtungen, aber auch deduktiv durch Ableitung aus Gesetzen oder gar einer Theorie gewonnen und müssen noch überprüft werden."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "685e5da0-d5b5-4e65-a0f0-4520943e7f02",
                                                "sense_id": "7f9ab0c4-be61-3b76-84fa-b12239ab204c",
                                                "text": "„Entscheidend ist, daß Phantasie und Einfallsreichtum auf glückliche Fragen und fruchtbare Hypothesen führen.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8ef32d5a-08f8-48ba-8827-546107c49ce9",
                                                "sense_id": "7f9ab0c4-be61-3b76-84fa-b12239ab204c",
                                                "text": "„Besteht die Hypothese diese Prüfung, dann hat man eine erste Theorie.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c420d979-3e94-44e6-8272-a194d39772d8",
                                                "sense_id": "7f9ab0c4-be61-3b76-84fa-b12239ab204c",
                                                "text": "„Die Ontologisierung linguistischer Konstrukte ist natürlich kein ausschließlich unbewußter Vorgang, sondern wird an verschiedenen Stellen bewußt durch zusätzliche Hypothesen vertreten.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4c2d93ca-fb4e-46b6-b6d9-921893826f9c",
                                                "sense_id": "7f9ab0c4-be61-3b76-84fa-b12239ab204c",
                                                "text": "„Hypothesen sind Netze, nur der wird fangen, der auswirft.“"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "bef63c66-f7bd-37b3-8505-8048512e5b5b",
                                        "entry_id": "e6eca988-a510-3c3a-b528-9cf4b6d8c9fd",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "bloße Annahme, Behauptung ohne Beleg"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "general"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5bddc2a3-6684-4be3-98b9-abbfa1044289",
                                                "sense_id": "bef63c66-f7bd-37b3-8505-8048512e5b5b",
                                                "text": "„Hypothesen sind Netze, nur der wird fangen, der auswirft.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "46c061ac-98f8-45df-b656-3b75da9e45a7",
                                                "sense_id": "bef63c66-f7bd-37b3-8505-8048512e5b5b",
                                                "text": "Seine Überlegungen sind pure Hypothesen, die durch nichts zu belegen sind."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "aa76d4f5-d752-497d-96f0-0865407b9462",
                                                "sense_id": "bef63c66-f7bd-37b3-8505-8048512e5b5b",
                                                "text": "„Jeder brachte neue Hypothesen an, und Nab begann zu weinen, weil man ihn nicht in seine geliebte Küche ließ.“"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"2\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "88b22dac-adab-402a-a9b3-eef46bbf7a92",
                        "source_entry_id": "bd8f512d-a666-325e-bd52-619cbe9ec433",
                        "target_lang_word": "hypothesis",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "hypothesis",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f126edc1-6ff3-3cf2-9dff-8ae30bbb82fe",
                                        "entry_id": "39c77eb2-6ed0-3c7a-b0ff-8a3df92afa32",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A tentative conjecture explaining an observation, phenomenon or scientific problem and that can be tested by further observation, investigation, and/or experimentation."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1722759e-97ba-4fbc-b843-811486d0f670",
                                                "sense_id": "f126edc1-6ff3-3cf2-9dff-8ae30bbb82fe",
                                                "text": "This hypothesis goes by many names, including group resistence, the threshold effect, and the gender paradox. Because the hypothesis holds such wide appeal, it is worth revisiting the logic behind it. The hypothesis is built on the factual observation that fewer females than males act antisocially."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9a28b0c7-29bd-43ee-8828-4935eb56fafc",
                                                "sense_id": "f126edc1-6ff3-3cf2-9dff-8ae30bbb82fe",
                                                "text": "Far too many of us have been taught in school that a scientist, in the course of trying to figure something out, will first come up with a \"hypothesis\" (a guess or surmise—not necessarily even an \"educated\" guess). ... [But t]he word \"hypothesis\" should be used, in science, exclusively for a reasoned, sensible, knowledge-informed explanation for why some phenomenon exists or occurs. An hypothesis can be as yet untested; can have already been tested; may have been falsified; may have not yet been falsified, although tested; or may have been tested in a myriad of ways countless times without being falsified; and it may come to be universally accepted by the scientific community. An understanding of the word \"hypothesis,\" as used in science, requires a grasp of the principles underlying Occam's Razor and Karl Popper's thought in regard to \"falsifiability\"—including the notion that any respectable scientific hypothesis must, in principle, be \"capable of\" being proven wrong (if it should, in fact, just happen to be wrong), but none can ever be proved to be true. One aspect of a proper understanding of the word \"hypothesis,\" as used in science, is that only a vanishingly small percentage of hypotheses could ever potentially become a theory."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f8f5b572-76a1-3793-9f22-de132b3c43d2",
                                        "entry_id": "39c77eb2-6ed0-3c7a-b0ff-8a3df92afa32",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An assumption taken to be true for the purpose of argument or investigation."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "general"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c1d604ee-1758-3a38-8d2f-7fb57dac41a1",
